error[E0521]: borrowed data escapes outside of closure
  --> tests/event_type_contracts/fail/callback_borrows.rs:14:44
   |
 9 |     let retained: Cell<Option<&'static State>> = Cell::new(None);
   |         -------- `retained` declared here, outside of the closure body
...
14 |             move |(state,), _, (), _scope| retained.set(Some(state)),
   |                                            ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ a temporary borrow escapes the closure body here
   |
   = help: `retained` is declared outside the closure, so any data borrowed inside the closure cannot be stored into it
   = note: requirement occurs because of the type `Cell<Option<&State>>`, which makes the generic argument `Option<&State>` invariant
   = note: the struct `Cell<T>` is invariant over the parameter `T`
   = help: see <https://doc.rust-lang.org/nomicon/subtyping.html> for more information about variance

